And okay, let's start with two
papers that are actually from my

00:10:28.643 --> 00:10:32.146
research group, the first one,
my model checker died,

00:10:32.147 --> 00:10:33.317
how well did it do?

00:10:33.318 --> 00:10:38.120
What it does basically,
it gives you a measure,

00:10:38.121 --> 00:10:41.514
it gives you a-
&gt;&gt; Do they have to go together?

00:10:41.515 --> 00:10:44.920
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH] Pretty much,
that's what you're asking, yeah?

00:10:44.921 --> 00:10:47.715
So it gives you some
probabilistic measure,

00:10:47.716 --> 00:10:48.528
why is that?

00:10:48.529 --> 00:10:53.236
Because it tackles probabilistic
model checking of Markov chains,

00:10:53.237 --> 00:10:53.811
right.

00:10:53.812 --> 00:10:56.912
And what it asks for the user
is the usage profile, so

00:10:56.913 --> 00:11:00.100
you need to give it some idea
