00:11:11.541 --> 00:11:16.343
But also, this does not really
scale that well to software

00:11:16.344 --> 00:11:19.612
model checking of
actual source code.

00:11:19.613 --> 00:11:23.217
Besides, it's super sensitive
to those usage profiles that you

00:11:23.218 --> 00:11:26.559
provide, so it's not ideal,
there's definitely room for

00:11:26.560 --> 00:11:27.419
improvement.

00:11:27.420 --> 00:11:30.884
Then alloy plus [INAUDIBLE],
alloy is a specification

00:11:30.885 --> 00:11:33.733
language that is
specifically suitable for

00:11:33.734 --> 00:11:37.660
structural properties, so
it's good to specify, maybe,

00:11:37.661 --> 00:11:39.587
data structure invariants.

00:11:39.588 --> 00:11:42.758
And the way it works is,
